NOTICE: --max-timeslice=100000 lets a thread that computes without a syscall run at most about 10000 retired conditional branches before a timer event stops it, and the guest is stepped through up to 2000 branches (the skid margin) to place each event, so a CPU-bound guest can run orders of magnitude slower than at the default (--max-timeslice=200000000), and a --timeout that expires may mean a slow run rather than a hung one. Omit --max-timeslice, or raise it, for a faster run; --summary reports how many timeslices the run had.
HERMIT_HOST_INPUT_CHANGED_SINCE_RECORDING stderr (fd 2) was a pipe in the recording and is a regular file now; the run may diverge where the guest checks it (fstat, isatty, fsync, lseek)
